## The starter contract

The app container (`{{appName}}`) runs the image built from the starter's `Dockerfile` (called `calm-service` here; the
overlay names the image built for the service). It must listen on `$PORT` ({{servicePort}}) and answer `GET /health`.
It is told:

| Variable | Value |
|---|---|
{{#each workloads}}
{{#if isApp}}
{{#each env}}
| `{{name}}` | `{{{value}}}` |
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/each}}

## Nodes in the cluster

| Name | Node | Technology | Image | Service port | Pod port |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{{#each workloads}}
| `{{k8sName}}` | {{name}} | {{{technology}}} | `{{image}}` | {{servicePort}} | {{containerPort}} |
{{/each}}
{{#if renamedWorkloads.length}}

These nodes' unique-ids are not valid Kubernetes names, so they run under a converted name: lower case, other
characters as `-`, `x-` in front when it would not start with a letter, and a short hash when two ids would get the
same name, the id is too long or it is a word YAML reads as a boolean or null. Their objects keep the unique-id in the
`calm.finos.org/unique-id` annotation.

| Node unique-id | Name |
|---|---|
{{#each renamedWorkloads}}
| `{{id}}` | `{{k8sName}}` |
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

The gateway's external address in the architecture is `{{gatewayHost}}:{{gatewayPort}}`. Inside the cluster it is
`{{gatewayNode}}:{{gatewayServicePort}}`.

